EVERY USDC HAS A PLACE

Simulation before fees. No wallet actions. Matched money waits for the result; unused backing is claimable after STOP. Claims never depend on another person claiming first.

Matched funds stay locked.

Even the platform operator cannot VOID a matched market before Ask Oracle.

From Ask, an operator can VOID an unresolved market without an Oracle answer. You can then claim your matched stake. Ask is not a settlement deadline or an automatic refund.

Unmatched backing unlocks at STOP, less its quoted charge. Earned fees stay paid.

02
Good vs. bad examples

Name the event, date, timezone and evidence source. Write what YES, NO and VOID mean before anyone bets.

Bad question
“Will there be a big earthquake tomorrow?”

How big? Where? Tomorrow in which timezone? Two people could read this differently.

Good question
“Will USGS record an earthquake of magnitude 5.0 or higher anywhere in the world on 1 December 2026, UTC?”

The USGS earthquake catalog is the source. Check the event’s occurrence time, from 00:00 up to the next midnight UTC.

YES — at least one qualifying event.
NO — the complete record shows none.
VOID — the record is unavailable or cannot establish the answer.

Example only. STOP closes bets; Ask Oracle should leave enough time for the evidence to appear. Public markets are not automatically vetted—read the question and every rule before funding.

